a, Media\nL91: # Code, Data and Media Associated with this Article\nL92: \nL93: [Input] alphaXiv Toggle\nL94: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[1704.04831] Smooth-supported multiplicative functions in arithmetic progressions beyond the $x^{1/2}$-barrier (https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.04831)\nciteturn9view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.04831\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2412.17583] Asymptotic independence of $Ω(n)$ and $Ω(n+1)$ along logarithmic averages (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.17583)\nciteturn9view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.17583\",\"lineno\":8}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Number Theory\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 23 Dec 2024 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 17 Aug 2026 (this version, v3)]\nL9: # Title:Asymptotic independence of $Ω(n)$ and $Ω(n+1)$ along logarithmic averages\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Dimitrios Charamaras , cite7†Florian K. Richter L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Asymptotic independence of $\\Omega(n)$ and $\\Omega(n+1)$ along logarithmic averages, by Dimitrios Charamaras and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Let $\\Omega(n)$ denote the number of prime factors of a positive integer $n$ counted with multiplicities. We show that for any bounded functions $a,b\\colon\\mathbb{N}\\to\\mathbb{C}$, $$\\frac{1}{\\log{N}}\\sum_{n=1}^N \\frac{a(\\Omega(n))b(\\Omega(n+1))}{n} = \\Bigg(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{n=1}^N a(\\Omega(n))\\Bigg)\\Bigg(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{n=1}^N b(\\Omega(n))\\Bigg) + \\mathrm{o}_{N\\to\\infty}(1).$$ This generalizes a theorem of Tao on the logarithmically averaged two-point correlation Chowla conjecture.\nL17: Our result is quantitative and the explicit error term that we obtain establishes double-logarithmic savings. As an application, we obtain new results about the distribution of $\\Omega(p+1)$ as $p$ ranges over $\\ell$-almost primes for a \"typical\" value of $\\ell$.\nL18: Comments:  | 43 pages, 3rd version (improvement of the error term in the main theorem; appendix added)\nL19: Subjects:  | Number Theory (math.NT)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 11N37 (Primary) 11K65 (Secondary)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2412.17583 [math.NT]\nL22:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2412.17583v3 [math.NT] for this version)\nL23:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2412.17583†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Dimitrios Charamaras [cite13†view email ]\nL27: cite5†[v1] Mon, 23 Dec 2024 13:55:14 UTC (37 KB)\nL28: cite14†[v2] Tue, 18 Feb 2025 13:26:11 UTC (37 KB)\nL29: [v3] Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:41:33 UTC (34 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled Asymptotic independence of $\\Omega(n)$ and $\\Omega(n+1)$ along logarithmic averages, by Dimitrios Charamaras and 1 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * cite8†View PDF L38:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite15†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite16†view license†creativecommons.org L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: math.NT\nL45: \nL46: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L47: \nL48: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2024-12 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite22†math L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite